{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs","id":1432925,"title":"Sure Why Not DBs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-21T10:58:51-08:00","id":1432925,"title":"Sure Why Not DBs","content":"Brief closing thoughts on the Well Bred Merit from an earlier thread. Having re-evaluated my thoughts I think I was wrong about what squicked me out about the merit.<br /> Having a lineage of heroes that is in some way predictable is fine. What bugs me is that the merit actually determines that as fact. It\u2019s not just a social rumor or supposition by the Realm\u2014it is a defined better odds. <br /> There being lineages is fine and a grand scale \u201cthis house has produced more Exalted then this one\u201d is okay, but once it comes down to the individual being more likely, it feels incredibly uncomfortable. The fact that it _isnt_ just socially useful in the Realm but anywhere adds to that. I don\u2019t feel comfortable with a character option being \u201cfactually my kids are more likely to exalt\u201d even if the main benefit is social.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T11:59:22-08:00","id":1432937,"title":"","content":"Why does that bother you?<br /> <br /> Some traits (IRL) are genetic. Some powers are inherited.<br /> <br /> The child of a god is more likely to be god-blooded than a child of a mortal.<br /> <br /> You have every right not to like this as a game element, I just don't understand why a character's children being factually more likely to Exalt as <i>Dragon-Blooded </i>makes you uncomfortable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T12:05:52-08:00","id":1432938,"title":"","content":"One thing I'll say is that doesn't really need to have anything to do with eugenics as the ideology has actually played out, particularly for having no element of forcibly sterilising anybody.<br /> <br /> It's really more like property inheritance, than anything. The policies of House Nellens having more in common with the Habsburgs accumulating half of Europe than anybody with an idea of promoting hereditary intelligence.<br /> <br /> I think it helps to have matters of the unExalted still having high quality Dragon's Blood that makes them desirable parents, and the inclusion of Terrestrial Exalted with physical disabilities. That and the elimination of any idea that there were ancient Dragon Blooded who could not produce mortal children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T12:23:31-08:00","id":1432939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1432937#post1432937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does that bother you?<br /> <br /> Some traits (IRL) are genetic. Some powers are inherited.<br /> <br /> The child of a god is more likely to be god-blooded than a child of a mortal.<br /> <br /> You have every right not to like this as a game element, I just don't understand why a character's children being factually more likely to Exalt as <i>Dragon-Blooded </i>makes you uncomfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So Dragonblooded being a hero of legacy etc isn't what bugs me. Families of Heroes, bending in Avatar, etc. Inherited Super Powers doesn't bug me. Dragonblooded parents being much more likely to have a dragonblooded kid than 2 mortals who's last DB was several generations ago doesn't bug me(I said something opposite earlier, and misattributed the discomfort).<br /> <br /> It is the Well Bred merit making your Dragonblooded Character even more likely to have dragonblooded children is what is uncomfortable. It is <i>specifically</i> the Well Bred and Thin Blooded Merits having something besides social implications (Not mechanically no--there isn't a roll to determine if your kid exalts--but in a still out of character knowledge sense, from the side bar) is the discomfort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T13:01:59-08:00","id":1432944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1432939#post1432939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So Dragonblooded being a hero of legacy etc isn't what bugs me. Families of Heroes, bending in Avatar, etc. Inherited Super Powers doesn't bug me. Dragonblooded parents being much more likely to have a dragonblooded kid than 2 mortals who's last DB was several generations ago doesn't bug me(I said something opposite earlier, and misattributed the discomfort).<br /> <br /> It is the Well Bred merit making your Dragonblooded Character even more likely to have dragonblooded children is what is uncomfortable. It is <i>specifically</i> the Well Bred and Thin Blooded Merits having something besides social implications (Not mechanically no--there isn't a roll to determine if your kid exalts--but in a still out of character knowledge sense, from the side bar) is the discomfort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is an issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T13:02:29-08:00","id":1432946,"title":"","content":"So is it that some dragonblooded parents are more likely to have exalted children, or even more specifically just the merit existing that you can give your character a better or worse chance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T13:46:11-08:00","id":1432952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1432944#post1432944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is an issue?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1432946#post1432946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is it that some dragonblooded parents are more likely to have exalted children, or even more specifically just the merit existing that you can give your character a better or worse chance?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The latter seems to be what rubs me the wrong way, yes. I think it's fine for a player to gain a benefit from the social expectations of a pedigree--it being a confirmed genuine thing bugs me more. <br /> Edited version of the Merit:<br /> <br /> The character has an exceptionally refined pedigree, and history is a predictor of the future. Her children are expected to Exalt as Dragon-Blooded, more so than her peers. This is a prized commodity within the Realm and throughout Creation. Whenever she makes a bargain roll in which her bloodline is a factor, such as negotiating a Dynastic marriage contract or bartering with the noble families of Nechara, she adds an automatic success. Conversely, she gains +1 Resolve against bargains in that context. Neither of these count as a bonus from Charms. <br /> <br /> Basically removing that, in fact, your character has better odds of having Exalted Children. That's the part that feels off and uncomfortable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":". 01-21-2021, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T13:55:41-08:00","id":1432956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1432952#post1432952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically removing that, in fact, your character has better odds of having Exalted Children. That's the part that feels off and uncomfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't tell me why it's an issue or uncomfortable. The point of the merit is that it gives a better perspective on what's the difference between the realm and lookshy in terms of dragon blooded numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T14:45:21-08:00","id":1432961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1432952#post1432952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically removing that, in fact, your character has better odds of having Exalted Children. That's the part that feels off and uncomfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you expand on this? Like why it\u2019s okay for some people to have better odds of having exalted children, but not good if the PCs do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T14:45:57-08:00","id":1432962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1432956#post1432956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't tell me why it's an issue or uncomfortable. The point of the merit is that it gives a better perspective on what's the difference between the realm and lookshy in terms of dragon blooded numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I don't see how it does that, can you elaborate? The Merit does not require being a part of the Realm or Lookshy, nor is it free for either character types at character Creation? And applies to all people in creation who care about it.<br /> &quot;Why is it an issue&quot; Mechanically it's not. In the earlier thread I commented on being dissappointed, not that it broke setting assumptions or was a bad wrong thing.<br /> &quot;Why it is uncomfortable for me&quot;...having a merit that concretely says &quot;your kids are more likely to exalt than other DBs&quot; feels weird, in that it focuses on children and gives a player concrete knowledge that feels like it shouldn't exist. It's extraneous information with no mechanical benefit (the exaltation of kids is ST fiat) that's just uncomfortably reminding you &quot;hey, people really care that you have kids and value you for your lineage in a concrete biological way&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T14:49:30-08:00","id":1432963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1432961#post1432961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you expand on this? Like why it\u2019s okay for some people to have better odds of having exalted children, but not good if the PCs do?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Kinda touched on above, but to elaborate:<br /> It's weird to spend merit points to have my kids more likely to exalt, because it's wierd to spend merit points on things for my kids. And I kinda feel like players shouldn't have control over the odds of Exaltation at all, except the Caul pilgrimage.<br /> I tihnk an example would be if beastmen merits called attention to your kids will also get your cat eyes or your thautmurgy. That'd be...weird and extraneous. Like yes, it is <i>factually true</i> that a character with cat eyes is more likely to have kids with cat eyes. Mentioning it is weird. <br /> Mentioning it in a merit who's main benefit is the social bargaining power the social pedigree brings--unless folks are doing blood tests--is a bit weirder to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T17:26:17-08:00","id":1432981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1432963#post1432963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda touched on above, but to elaborate:<br /> It's weird to spend merit points to have my kids more likely to exalt, because it's wierd to spend merit points on things for my kids. And I kinda feel like players shouldn't have control over the odds of Exaltation at all, except the Caul pilgrimage.<br /> I tihnk an example would be if beastmen merits called attention to your kids will also get your cat eyes or your thautmurgy. That'd be...weird and extraneous. Like yes, it is <i>factually true</i> that a character with cat eyes is more likely to have kids with cat eyes. Mentioning it is weird.<br /> Mentioning it in a merit who's main benefit is the social bargaining power the social pedigree brings--unless folks are doing blood tests--is a bit weirder to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it might not be so much that people are doing blood tests, but there's an entire ministry of the imperial government dedicated to tracking people's blood strength. If you can prove all 32 of your great grand dai-parents were exalted that's pretty good. You have strong blood, the dragon fire runs really hot in it, and that does translate to your kids.<br /> <br /> It also may actually affect a game. I'm not sure if it was mentioned in What Fire Has Wrought, since it didn't have an ST section, but in 2e's Manual of Exalted Power: Dragonblooded had a suggestion for a generational game. Where you play one character for a time, then skip time forward and play their kids, then again and play THEIR kids, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T18:02:10-08:00","id":1432984,"title":"","content":"I will point out the well-bred merit only applies in situation. negotiations, where your bloodline would matter. So not like you're gonna be gaining advantages to battle strategy because you come from a long line of DBs. <br /> <br /> Now while it isn't exactly spelled out, I would assume that the merit means not only do you have this, but that you possess or a way exists whereby people can verify this lineage. Not just that people look at you and go &quot;Yup that one's got exalt birthin loins.&quot; Note there is a sidebar right after thin blood mentioning that it is still a rather imprecise science, lineages with excellent breeding still have a 20% chance for their kids to be mortal, maybe half for averages, not counting weird stuff where a wild swing happens and none of some great bloodline's 8 children exalt with a bunch of exalts coming from some really happy mortal dynast couple. And ultimately its an at the table call if it comes up. <br /> <br /> So this would be a situation wherein you're negotiating your blood is in play. Maybe you're negotiating your marriage into a family for some asset and you're presenting your great odds of producing exalted children as why House Mnemon should consider letting you marry that scion of the house that you really hit it off with during a Wyld Hunt despite the fact that your character is from some random bloody satrapy in the sticks as far as the Dynasts are concerned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T18:24:26-08:00","id":1432985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1432962#post1432962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...I don't see how it does that, can you elaborate? The Merit does not require being a part of the Realm or Lookshy, nor is it free for either character types at character Creation? And applies to all people in creation who care about it.<br /> &quot;Why is it an issue&quot; Mechanically it's not. In the earlier thread I commented on being dissappointed, not that it broke setting assumptions or was a bad wrong thing.<br /> &quot;Why it is uncomfortable for me&quot;...having a merit that concretely says &quot;your kids are more likely to exalt than other DBs&quot; feels weird, in that it focuses on children and gives a player concrete knowledge that feels like it shouldn't exist. It's extraneous information with no mechanical benefit (the exaltation of kids is ST fiat) that's just uncomfortably reminding you &quot;hey, people really care that you have kids and value you for your lineage in a concrete biological way&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's reminding you that the Realm values this trait to an absurd degree for a reason. The merit is saying it does have real applications. That outside the realm and parsad, dragon blooded have less exalted children and the reason. Merits like this one don't inform the character of anything. This is an out of world statement to indicate to a player or an ST that if the character they make lives in the realm they can expect more dragon blooded children. However, if they're outside of it, it'll be rare even with another dragon-blooded as their partner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T18:26:52-08:00","id":1432986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1432952#post1432952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically removing that, in fact, your character has better odds of having Exalted Children.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it leads back into the question of how this was ever an expectation and why characters believe it if it never bears out. It makes them look exceptionally unobservant about a thing that is of key interest to them and that they're surrounded by.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1432952#post1432952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Why it is uncomfortable for me&quot;...having a merit that concretely says &quot;your kids are more likely to exalt than other DBs&quot; feels weird, in that it focuses on children and gives a player concrete knowledge that feels like it shouldn't exist. It's extraneous information with no mechanical benefit (the exaltation of kids is ST fiat) that's just uncomfortably reminding you &quot;hey, people really care that you have kids and value you for your lineage in a concrete biological way&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the Realm is meant to be full of uncomfortable things on that count. It's why Dynasts can't select who they marry. It's why gay Dynasts have a few pressures against living comfortably. It's why men who have extramarital children get a hard time for it.<br /> <br /> What is uncomfortable there functions as a source of drama and tension that is part of the game's commentary on power. <br /> <br /> And it levies a cost for acting in-character against that source of discomfort. Being Well Bred gives you social power, it can give you greater political power from the Exalted children you'll have authority over, it perpetuates the Great House, but it comes with a restriction on autonomy. You can decide autonomy matters more to you, but you give something up for it.<br /> <br /> It removes some of the teeth from that narrative to say you're not really giving anything up at all.<br /> <br /> (The other side is that Exalted does not shy away from letting you be morally compromised to exert power. You can learn sorcery from Mara.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1432963#post1432963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tihnk an example would be if beastmen merits called attention to your kids will also get your cat eyes or your thautmurgy. That'd be...weird and extraneous.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, that is a lot less significant to the narrative of beastfolk than it is to the magic aristocrats. If the Dragon Blooded are going to be magic aristocrats, it's going to cover all the bases.<br /> <br /> On the other, there is a sidebar talking about how impregnation while a Lunar is in their hybrid form will probably result in the child inheriting mutations, because Lunars actually do cover some parts of animal-human crossbreed narratives, even if it's way less prominent there.<br /> <br /> Lunars instead give prominence to narratives such as murdering people in order to assume their appearance.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It's a matter of how Exalted as a game is about taking these elements from fantasy and myth and history and giving some examination to their implications. It doesn't quite make moral judgement, but it doesn't shy away from the uncomfortable stuff. It sympathises with character motivations to do so, but doesn't rationalise them.<br /> <br /> Dragon Blooded are given motive to perform this stuff with substance, and the issues with it are apparent in text. The player is empowered to engage with those motives and challenges they present, one way or another. It is... less elaborate to present the setup but give it no reality, or not invite players to take part in the dialogue about it.<br /> <br /> The Well Bred Merit is not an endorsement of the Realm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 01-21-2021, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T19:11:06-08:00","id":1432994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1432963#post1432963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's weird to spend merit points to have my kids more likely to exalt, because it's wierd to spend merit points on things for my kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Selective Conception merit bothers me for the same reason-- your character having kids (destined to Exalt or not) is such a significant character development that it should always be the player's choice. Like, even a &quot;kid they never knew they had&quot; plot should be run by the player first. I, for one, would be kind of uncomfortable if the GM pulled that on me out of nowhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T19:47:10-08:00","id":1432998,"title":"","content":"Selective Conception is not an out-of-character meta thing, though. It's a Merit in which the character has the actual trait of controlling their conception deliberately.<br /> <br /> Questions of how pregnancy is handled can reasonably differ between players, but even in a game where everybody is in a place of &quot;this happens only if we want it to&quot;, there's additional narrative space for a character having actively switched it on.<br /> <br /> That's how you get stories such as Dune, where there's an apparent political flex and impending succession crisis to the emperor's Bene Gesserit consort having given him only daughters.<br /> <br /> For Well Bred, I take issue with phrasing it as spending Merit points on children while also recognising the social influence elements of it. You're spending points for the dice bonuses representing the regard people will place on your established capacity to provide Exalted children.<br /> <br /> That gives it tighter narrative focus than the Breeding Background, which provided larger mote pools and eventually access to additional Charms. Exclusivity producing Dragon Blooded who were actually more powerful, <i>there's</i> some eugenics stuff to get up in arms about (not to mention a Background that ends up feeling kind of mandatory but not actually very interesting).<br /> <br /> The Well Bred Merit, you buy that if you want to engage with the intrigue of people pursuing you as a marriage prospect because of the promise of your children. Or if you want the advantage if that's going to be part of the game anyway.<br /> <br /> Heck, take the Merit and then demand that none of your children Exalt. That's part of how it can work in the setting!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T20:24:54-08:00","id":1433005,"title":"","content":"Why is it bad? I mean, yes, it's uncomfortable, but that's kind of the thing. Having bloodline and family-based superpowers and having 'I am a descendant of the king and thus am the rightful king!' is the sort of thing DBs have, and yes, it's uncomfortable because that's a deliberate examination of what it can mean. <br /> <br /> It's like the words: &quot;A happy slave is a broken slave.&quot; <br /> <br /> Besides. That would also make the superhumans of the Realm profoundly unobservant and dumb. What, is the people who can throw around 20 or so dice on pattern recognition and incapable of recognising that their eugenics efforts have no effect on the rates of Exaltation, when normal scientists can figure it out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T20:26:06-08:00","id":1433006,"title":"","content":"Feudalist propaganda around a blood-based ruling class of 'betters', supremacist thinking of 'the chosen race', and the nepotism accompanying each are, to modern meritocratic thinking, abhorrent. The arranged marriages and the wasting of human talent for the accident of their birth, doubly so. To have a mechanic such as Well-Bred whiffs of the widespread glorification of oppressors. <br /> <br /> This, in certain society-changing campaigns, is a challenge to the players to imagine something better. Do you promote people based on their ability to recall the words of a certain philosopher in written exams? Do you allow the most ruthless exploiters of labor to accrue the capital they will use to buy and market their own positions of privilege? Do you allow the abbots of the Immaculate Order or Cult of the Illuminated to take the levels of state power and assert a theocracy? Keep in mind that the Dragon-Blooded will still, mechanically, best mortals in these selection mechanisms (Celestial Exalted, better still). Because the world of Exalted is intentionally biased, lacking in fairness, unapologetically hierarchical. <br /> <br /> On a more personal basis, being uncomfortable about your peers or elders having an interest, let alone voicing it to you, about your own procreation decisions can, indeed, be stressful. But telling off or besting that NPC is the catharsis such tension sets up. In that way, Exalted can be the healthy practice of setting and keeping boundaries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T20:58:20-08:00","id":1433010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1433006#post1433006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feudalist propaganda around a blood-based ruling class of 'betters'</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite convinced that this has ever exactly been a thing, at least in quite the terms being discussed here.<br /> <br /> The arranged marriages and the wasting of human talent for the accident of their birth, doubly so. To have a mechanic such as Well-Bred whiffs of the widespread glorification of oppressors. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you promote people based on their ability to recall the words of a certain philosopher in written exams? Do you allow the most ruthless exploiters of labor to accrue the capital they will use to buy and market their own positions of privilege? Do you allow the abbots of the Immaculate Order or Cult of the Illuminated to take the levels of state power and assert a theocracy? Keep in mind that the Dragon-Blooded will still, mechanically, best mortals in these selection mechanisms (Celestial Exalted, better still).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of accurate in the aggregate, the most zoomed out perspective in the setting, but ends up losing a lot of details in how the setting is depicted and would logically function from character design and common sense.<br /> <br /> Some of those are things where a direct measurable competition isn't really the most sensible way for them to work, and some are where there are enough configurations of people that it becomes perfectly suitable to have places where an Exalt of particular skills and inclination interacts with several mortals who are better at certain things.<br /> <br /> Or good at things complementary to the Exalt.<br /> <br /> Or less good at things but are compelling to an Exalt, in ways that can make Exalted power serve agendas not their own.<br /> <br /> The Touman Clans have a Lunar who does not lead them (even though she probably has leadership skills), and is in a position where she might do things that serve the mortal leader rather than herself.<br /> <br /> Even in the Scarlet Dynasty, this nuance can be found. Prominently in House Nellens, but even elsewhere there can be a mortal better at something important than a Dragon Blood, or where the nature of their relationship complicates the power dynamic (even if their society functions on an assumption of Exalted at the top).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T22:31:13-08:00","id":1433014,"title":"","content":"It still can get pretty uncomfortable though. One of the core premises of Exalted is that the exalts are vastly more skilled than mortals. They can more easily achieve the greatest human feats, and almost casually surpass them. The dragonblooded have that as inherited power that is 100% to do with their bloodline and the purity of it, how many previous people with magic powers are in their ancestor book and how pure their blood was.<br /> <br /> You could dismantle all of their real world like inherited power and aristocratic oppression, and you'd still be left with family lines that live for centuries, and are the greatest generals, bureaucrats, orators, artists, thieves and doctors in the world. In a lot of ways they really are just better, just not morally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T02:24:52-08:00","id":1433028,"title":"","content":"Dragon Blooded families could over time engage in pairings that would distribute the Essence so widely that you'd only ever get them popping up out of nowhere, although coercing them into that actually would be eugenics.<br /> <br /> Mind, I think it would not need to be coercive if the attitude towards power was changed so that they did not prioritise organising themselves like that, but that's a bigger thing for the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T03:26:14-08:00","id":1433032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1433028#post1433028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon Blooded families could over time engage in pairings that would distribute the Essence so widely that you'd only ever get them popping up out of nowhere, although coercing them into that actually would be eugenics.<br /> <br /> Mind, I think it would not need to be coercive if the attitude towards power was changed so that they did not prioritise organising themselves like that, but that's a bigger thing for the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>They... can? <br /> <br /> Yes, but why would they? Dragonblooded are incredible, especially on a mortal scale. Even on the scale of the gods they can train themselves up to gain more and more superpowers. They're human, tied to human views, have flexibility, and can combine together to get bigger effects. Human beings carried out incest to absurd degrees (like the Hapsburgs and Ptolemy) just to keep power and wealth in the family. <br /> <br /> How much more for true blue superpowers? Powers, in a world where mortals are often the weakest things sentient beings? Remember. Dragonblooded are the weakest of the Exalted, and are still a heads and shoulders above mortals in things they put their mind to. It is fundamentally unlikely they will change to anything that would cause less DBs to be made, because that means being fucked over by those with more Dragonblooded scions, but also the myraid of monsters like fae, other humans, Behemoths, ghosts, and etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T04:07:43-08:00","id":1433035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1433032#post1433032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They... can?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a question or an agreement with uncertainty?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but why would they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Encouragement to follow their own hearts. Encouragement to not be so hung up on concentrated clans. Maybe effective promotion of an idea that a safer Creation will come from the Dragon's Blood being distributed in a manner that results in greater occurrence from the wider population.<br /> <br /> Could be a thing Dragon Blooded propose as an alternative to enemies who want to persecute them into destruction and have become strong enough to make a game attempt at it. Killing off the Scarlet Dynasty actually would jeopardize their numbers in the world, put a lot of that power to waste. There's an ancient Lunar trying to find a targeted means of wiping them out.<br /> <br /> Somebody could establish authority over the Dynasty and make such policies mandatory. Devastation of the Realm could leave them so widely dispersed that parenting children with mortals becomes the only option available.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragonblooded are incredible, especially on a mortal scale. Even on the scale of the gods they can train themselves up to gain more and more superpowers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this to be a response that misses the point of my statement that their whole attitude to power ought to change.<br /> <br /> I mean, yes, they'd be giving something up for it. It's a question of convincing people that those things shouldn't be valued that way in the first place. Some of that can be empathy, bringing people around on it leading to abuses that you feel bad about (or are inherently destabilising). Some of it can be appeals to their own well-being; is getting tangled up in these games really fulfilling for them? Are they happy? If happiness is not a thing they want, why?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human beings carried out incest to absurd degrees (like the Hapsburgs and Ptolemy) just to keep power and wealth in the family.</div> </div> </div> </div>Egypt amounts to all of one culture that ever translated this thing in terms of sibling marriages, and I am somewhat sceptical of the narrative surrounding that hereditary birth defect.<br /> <br /> That said, it's not really relevant, the Scarlet Dynasty has never been depicted as particularly dependant on or invested in incest as a means of continuing themselves.<br /> <br /> If you're contesting that two Dynast siblings, in the absence of any other options, would have children with one another for the sake of the bloodline, I would be sceptical of that conclusion being comprehensive, but also of that premise being particularly noteworthy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Powers, in a world where mortals are often the weakest things sentient beings? Remember. Dragonblooded are the weakest of the Exalted, and are still a heads and shoulders above mortals in things they put their mind to. It is fundamentally unlikely they will change to anything that would cause less DBs to be made, because that means being fucked over by those with more Dragonblooded scions, but also the myraid of monsters like fae, other humans, Behemoths, ghosts, and etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, the premise here is lowering the value of power over other people by reasons either empathetic or pragmatic.<br /> <br /> It's like Lord of the Rings. Sauron loses because he makes contingencies against enemies wanting to usurp his power while being unable to conceive that they'd want it so that nobody can use his power.<br /> <br /> Also, the premise as you've presented it has some faults. Thin blooded Terrestrials could have a means of banding together in opposition of a family unit, a Dragon Blooded family can over time be made less capable of reliable Exaltation in its children, the world as a whole can benefit from the fact that there are thousands of outcastes around.<br /> <br /> Cooperation with the other Exalted can start reviving those systems that concentrate power strategically. Although really, that's already how the Realm works; they don't evenly distribute their Dragon Blooded around the world to contest all the boogeymen, they keep them at home and use efficient systems of deployment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T04:16:27-08:00","id":1433036,"title":"","content":"Oh also, the setting presents the Confederation of Rivers as a sizable territory that does not and cannot utilise the systems of the Realm and ends up necessitating more mutual respect between mortals, gods and Exalted, and it not only thrives, it does so in the face of the Realm's hostility.<br /> <br /> The River Province has its own deep rooted problems with distribution of and attitudes towards power, but it's kind of contrary to the assertion that the group with the reliable Dragon Blooded inheritance overwhelms the one that doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T09:46:02-08:00","id":1433063,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the River Province, here's an interesting thing to speculate upon:<br /> <br /> The way it's depicted to us, vastly more of the outcastes of the Scavenger Lands go to Lookshy to submit for military service, rather than Nexus to make their fortunes.<br /> <br /> What ideas would people have as to why that is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T14:30:41-08:00","id":1433099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1432952#post1432952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically removing that, in fact, your character has better odds of having Exalted Children.</div> </div> </div> </div>And thereby instead making them the dud with three Exalted siblings and six Exalted aunts and uncles but only two Exalted children. If we\u2019re talking about merits that are off and uncomfortable I\u2019d say it\u2019s hard to do better than paying two dots to disappoint your family.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T23:14:21-08:00","id":1433142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1433099#post1433099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And thereby instead making them the dud with three Exalted siblings and six Exalted aunts and uncles but only two Exalted children. If we\u2019re talking about merits that are off and uncomfortable I\u2019d say it\u2019s hard to do better than paying two dots to disappoint your family.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ouch. Now I'm thinking of the Exalted grandmother, only this time she's asking how many exalted children you've got. <br /> <br /> &quot;When are they going to exalt? Oh, another dud? When are you going to give us more dragonblooded? We've been waiting for a long time.&quot; <br /> <br /> Only far more uncomfortable and dehumanizing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-23T02:48:54-08:00","id":1433151,"title":"","content":"At least with the current system, that number of Exalted children for the Well-Bred is an outlier. Rumours are probably inevitable, but there can be a few sensible people who understand that sometimes these things just happen, and at least the unExalted children can carry the Blood forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T09:57:14-08:00","id":1433515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1433206-starmetal-quantities-from-gods?p=1433482#post1433482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with an ironic juxtaposition like that is that it ignores both the power disparity between Celestial Exalted and Dragon-Blooded</div> </div> </div> </div>If one wants to make an argument about the mechanical representation being insufficient for their credibility, that would be one thing, but to the best of my knowledge the setting and character writing never presented the Scarlet Dynasty and the Realm as anything other than major powers in the setting worth taking seriously. I would find that to be the greater detail in determining the motives behind the writing in Exalted: the Sidereals.<br /> <br /> Still, I wasn't there seventeen years ago, I can't know for sure whether or not there were divisions among the writers based on petty fandom drama that would provide a context in which to read how the book presents divine attitudes towards Terrestrial Exalted. All I have to go on there is the fact that Geoff Grabowski is credited as developer of both books, and I would find it really weird for him to be taking swipes at himself (or insufficient to preventing the writers from doing so).<br /> <br /> Absent any of those qualifiers, it would still very much look to me like most of the line up to that point having presented the Dragon Blooded as a big deal in the world, and then having a later book pull back the curtain on Heaven to depict the gods as, among other unflattering qualities, an even older and more hidebound aristocracy that is distinctly unimpressed with the reigning Exalted.<br /> <br /> And to be perfectly frank, some of the archived forum conversations from those almost two decades ago or contrasting text against ways that people still talk about subjects after all of this time gives me an impression that there are more than a few ways that people's reads on things were distorted even at the time by an approach to Exalted: the Sidereals that was a bit touchy and would be reinforced by the intervening time.<br /> <br /> I'm saying this based on my best guess as to what the significance of the power disparity between Celestial and Terrestrial Exalted is to this subject. If I'm wrong I would appreciate clarity on what it refers to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">as well as the different ways they experience prejudice.</div> </div> </div> </div>What ways do they experience prejudice?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T17:29:47-08:00","id":1433557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1433515#post1433515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If one wants to make an argument about the mechanical representation being insufficient for their credibility, that would be one thing, but to the best of my knowledge the setting and character writing never presented the Scarlet Dynasty and the Realm as anything other than major powers in the setting worth taking seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about that, I'm talking about Dragon-Blooded as individuals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What ways do they experience prejudice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Celestial Exalts in Creation are subject to discrimination in Creation as people given great power that others think are demons.<br /> <br /> Historically, when that\u2019s flipped for Dragon-Blooded the focus is on inheriting the sins their ancestors or being unworthy of the same respect afforded to other Exalts due to their inherent inferiority. That\u2019s way more in line with people\u2019s lived experiences.<br /> <br /> Also, I believe the narrative of Dragon-Blooded as slaves who had the audacity to overthrow their superior masters started with Exalted: the Sidereals.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exalted the Sidereals page 19</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> While they are in Yu-Shan, Dragon-Blooded and mortals are living property, like a pet or familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T17:36:24-08:00","id":1433558,"title":"","content":"I think the lack of irony there is from the fact that Dragonblooded actually are lesser. Like if heaven treated Solars like they do mortals that's ironic because Solars are definitely not that. It would be silly, and pretty funny, if Heaven decided that the Solars should be lumped in with mortals as a class of being. With Terrestrials though they're just one step up, so it could kind of make sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> It also really doesn't help that most people's main interaction with the setting is through games, not through reading the books. Which means that the books can talk about how badass the Dragonblooded are until the world runs out of ink and it wouldn't matter. In play the mighty army of the Realm arrives with a dozen elite dragonblooded warriors and thousands of soldiers, and then the Dawn kills them to a one so fast that there's some PCs in the party who don't even get to take a turn.<br /> <br /> So in the last year the players read 3 pages about how awesome the Dynasts were, and then spent over 200 hours playing a game where they clown them like Bruce Lee vs a bunch of kindergartners. Then other fluff books come out with the idea that it's funny that Heaven treats Dragonblooded like they suck, okay, but anyone who's been playing the game weekly for years knows that's absolutely true.<br /> <br /> It'd be like having a setting book for DnD's Waterdeep that makes a joke about an army of a full <u><b><i>100 hobgoblins</i></b></u> headed for the city, and Laeral Silverhand is too disinterested to even get off her chair*. Even if a book told you that hobgoblins are an existential threat to Waterdeep, you just look at the stats and remember all the times you schooled them with your level 5 characters and it falls flat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *for those who don't follow DnD Laeral Silverhand could end an army of 100 hobgoblins in a single action, and Waterdeep the city has an elite army of griffon cavalry, a resident hero force which is basically fantasy Avengers, several adventuring guilds and groups, titanic animated stone statues, druid enclaves, ancient inhumanly powerful warrior monks, and dozens of other defenders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-26T22:29:55-08:00","id":1433579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1433063#post1433063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of the River Province, here's an interesting thing to speculate upon:<br /> <br /> The way it's depicted to us, vastly more of the outcastes of the Scavenger Lands go to Lookshy to submit for military service, rather than Nexus to make their fortunes.<br /> <br /> What ideas would people have as to why that is?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that could be as simple as advertising. &quot;Come to Lookshy and join the Seventh Legion! Be showered with money and privilege! Enjoy camaraderie with the only people who can ever really understand you! Open up cans of whoopass on demons, the undead, and other enemies of Creation!&quot; If I had just taken the Second Breath as a Terrestrial, that would be an awfully compelling pitch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T13:48:43-08:00","id":1433652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1433558#post1433558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In play the mighty army of the Realm arrives with a dozen elite dragonblooded warriors and thousands of soldiers, and then the Dawn kills them to a one so fast that there's some PCs in the party who don't even get to take a turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to focus on every play report that brings back results contrary to this so that the entire thing does not become fucking pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T15:34:56-08:00","id":1433660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1433652#post1433652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am going to focus on every play report that brings back results contrary to this so that the entire thing does not become fucking pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could, but that's not most people's experience from what I've heard and seen. There was a time in my last 2e campaign where a sworn brotherhood of 5 Essence 4-5 dragonblooded with several martial arts, including Crimson Pentacle Blade style, the one designed to be a force multiplier if multiple practitioners use it, challenged my Dawn to a 5v1 execution match. I just told the rest of the group to let me have them, and then looked to the ST and asked if we were really going to roll this out, he said no and we skipped to me dusting my hands off after thrashing them.<br /> <br /> Which was made worse, again just from what I've heard and seen at tables myself, by both STs and players trying to make it not...that. Okay, what if I make an immaculate monk, they're supposed to be the best of the best, Solar hunters, ultimate badasses. Nope, no dice, still die like mooks. What if I really lean into the artifacts, give my fire aspect the Eye of the Fire Dragon, the artifact 5 anti-solar spear. Heck, Oadenol's Codex even says, and I quote directly, &quot;A Dragonblooded warrior with the Eye of the Fire Dragon should be a true nightmare to the Solar Exalted.&quot; Guess what? They don't even warrant wasting time rolling Join Battle.<br /> <br /> You can see how in that context the joke might not really land when you print that the gods consider terrestrial exalted to be trash. Unless you've been playing mortal games where you're battling against Dragonblooded opponents, or Dragonblooded games where you're battling mortal opponents and not Solars, you have no reason to believe that isn't a perfectly valid opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-27T17:19:25-08:00","id":1433665,"title":"","content":"I found in the circles I frequented, what saved opinions of Dragon-Blooded was Abyssals.<br /> <br /> The Terrestrial Exalted generally managed to have the dignity of people who knew they'd only get the one life and didn't particularly want to lose it, occasionally you\u2019d get a fanatic but mostly they\u2019d reach a point where they\u2019d do the smart thing and walk away.<br /> <br /> Abyssals meanwhile had a distinct lack of dignity. They were close enough to Solar power level to justify excessive force but thematically the typical Deathknight was making huge sacrifices to be forever one step behind. Most importantly, they\u2019d often be way more afraid of going back to their Deathlord empty handed and make some doomed last stand to build heat for the real villain rather than allowing themselves to be captured.<br /> <br /> Now there's ways to do all of that respectfully... but remember, these were the guys with the BDSM themed martial art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 01-27-2021, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T21:07:14-08:00","id":1433767,"title":"","content":"... wow.<br /> <br /> I suppose things like that is why I have some issue communicating with those among my players who started in 2e, rather than in 1e as me and my oldest friends have; it's just. It's just something else. When I first started playing, Abyssals were powerful, and sexy, and half of my initial circle were Abyssal characters; the narrative of Death's encroachment upon Creation is a major one in games I am in or run to this day.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Blooded were always a dangerous thing to face; you could never trust that fighting powerful Immaculates wouldn't have your weapon hampered by Earth, and you could never easily dispatch a Water one, what with Bottomless Depths Defense. And hell, things like Safety Among Enemies meant they had endless lives as long as they had people around them. Facing a big force from the Realm or Lookshy was always a nightmare, mitigated only by getting powerful beings on your side, with 2nd Circle Demon or dealings with spirits being a great equalizer.<br /> <br /> Hell, one of the strongest combat characters in one of my first groups, a mostly Celestial group, was a CMA-using DB.<br /> <br /> I have mostly skipped 2e, and this, to me, really underscores how different editions may as well be completely different planets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 01-29-2021, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T07:36:18-08:00","id":1433792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1433767#post1433767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have mostly skipped 2e, and this, to me, really underscores how different editions may as well be completely different planets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, although worth pointing out is that much of the setting material didn\u2019t act like this was the case. It\u2019s just that level 2 stunts were trivial to get and awarded 2 motes back, and Solars had an easy to grab 3 mote perfect defence that negated any attack. Conversely the Dragonblooded had an 8m 1wp perfect that failed against any attack made or enhanced by magic, including just one mote of the first excellency. <br /> <br /> So your DB uses Uber mega charms to make 10 instant death attacks with 30 dice on each attack roll and the Solar just uses 10 Seven Shadow Evasions, or one with Leaping Dodge, and stunts it to pay less than 10 motes to perfectly avoid all attacks. Then they respond with their own perfect attack which due to the fact that it\u2019s charm enhanced the DB has no way at all to defend against it, not even apply their DV, and they explode. Which is why the only actual fights were basically solar on solar fights. <br /> <br /> 2.5e helped in that it increased the cost of perfects so at least you\u2019d run out sooner, but it was also so late in the game line that the Solars had years of racking up the scoreboard with supplemental material that made them more and more awesome so it didn\u2019t ultimately change all that much. For example by that time you could grab Essence 7 charms and be Essence 5 right off of your chargen, and that was hands down the most efficient way to build a character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T07:58:53-08:00","id":1433796,"title":"","content":"A 2 dice stunt actually gave 4m. A Solar could dodge that death-combo and GAIN 10m.<br /> <br /> (A 1 die stunt gave 2m.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T10:16:09-08:00","id":1433807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1433796#post1433796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A 2 dice stunt actually gave 4m. A Solar could dodge that death-combo and GAIN 10m.<br /> <br /> (A 1 die stunt gave 2m.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh right, yeah 2e was dumb. <br /> <br /> With this weapon, the very eye of Hesish himself, you will be a nightmare to the Solar Exalted. Crafted at the height of the high first age with a singular purpose, the spirit within it knows not other existence but to kill the chosen of the sun. No lawgiver could ever sleep soundly knowing one of the Dragonblooded armed with this spear seeks them. Unless they know how to stunt involving a part of the environment, in which case they\u2019ll dodge any attack made by it and receive a mote for the trouble. Or stunt in any way and all and just use a flurry breaker or their massive mote pool to negate the danger. We\u2019re still going to act like the setting considers DBs to be dangerous though until pretty bear the end of the game line where we\u2019ll start printing fluff that reflects the mechanics rather than fix the mechanics to reflect the fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T12:12:00-08:00","id":1433820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1433767#post1433767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... wow.<br /> <br /> I suppose things like that is why I have some issue communicating with those among my players who started in 2e, rather than in 1e as me and my oldest friends have; it's just. It's just something else. When I first started playing, Abyssals were powerful, and sexy, and half of my initial circle were Abyssal characters; the narrative of Death's encroachment upon Creation is a major one in games I am in or run to this day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm mostly talking about Abyssals as antagonists.<br /> Maybe having Abyssal PCs around overshadowed it but the Deathlords being the sort of masters you couldn't afford to fail sure as hell didn't start with 2nd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T12:51:52-08:00","id":1433827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1432925-sure-why-not-dbs?p=1433820#post1433820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mostly talking about Abyssals as antagonists.<br /> Maybe having Abyssal PCs around overshadowed it but the Deathlords being the sort of masters you couldn't afford to fail sure as hell didn't start with 2nd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not been that much of a thing in the circles I've played, sorry; Abyssals are a rare resource they have spent quite a bit into and would never just discard or waste, and while failing them likely involves some amount of torture, so does failing Mnemon, or the Yozi (Yozi-aligned opponents were always far more likely to be the way you describe, given how much the Yozi are fueled by rage and spite but even then... I guess the people I played with just gave more dignity to the setting, as a general rule?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T13:59:03-08:00","id":1433833,"title":"","content":"Okay, but since this was being framed as an edition change the first incident of this nature I've encountered is in Caste Book Night where White Bone Sinner gets tortured in some unspeakable way by Walker in Darkness for his failure to stop Jiunan Nightwarden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T14:10:06-08:00","id":1433835,"title":"","content":"It does feel like one? The people I know from 1e were there with me when Abyssals were one of, if not the, most popular splat, people who come in from 2e tend to take a very dim view of them, generally, due the way their MoEP sold them short. Exalted: the Abyssals certainly referred to the relationship between Deathknights and Deathlord as having such roles as a 'patron, teacher, confessor' and took pains to note how few Exaltations each Deathlord possessed and how much work it was to train each Deathknight.<br /> <br /> The lack of dignity you mention was certainly not there in how Abyssals were talked about in, say, RPG.net in the pre-2e times; maybe it's also not a thing in 2e, and it's mostly a thing with your group? Because it was certainly not a memetic thing in 1e that they lacked dignity. They were, in the talks about them in RPG.net, the Freedom Stone forums, and the like, viewed as powerful, sexy, dangerous, all that jazz.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 01-29-2021, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T15:36:31-08:00","id":1433848,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of Cool Goth Abyssals came from the fans. (Who were, by and large, VtM converts who wanted to play characters who were awesome.)<br /> <br /> 2E certainly sold Abyssals short, but Lioness literally just reference the published 1E text.<br /> <br /> I don't think anyone would deny that 2E treated Abyssals badly or exaggerated the problem. But it's something 2E magnified, not started. <br /> <br /> Exalted: The Abyssals (p111) says if a Deathknight fails &quot;Deathlords typically spare no opportunity to abuse and dishonor them.&quot; It also describes what an Abyssal is on p107: Cool Goth Solar is fanon. Page 113 to 115 describes the various ways a Deathlord can punish an Abyssal.<br /> <br /> But you're right, 1E Abyssals probably were the most popular splat until 2E stuck the knife in. 2E definitely made things worse, but it's not responsible for the idea of your Deathlord master being a dick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 01-30-2021, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-29T15:41:44-08:00","id":1433849,"title":"","content":"If you looked at forum discourse during 2e you probably wouldn't think almost a third of MoEP: Infernals was widely considered beyond saving. The fun people had with them as PCs overshadowed vastly larger flaws there. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-30T13:11:06-08:00","id":1433950,"title":"","content":"Since infernals are already confirmed to be going their own direction this edition, I'm still looking for a spiritual successor to the beautiful, weird, drug trip that was the charms section of the infernals book, devil tigers, and the fanbase surrounding those two. It was a trip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T02:37:44-08:00","id":1433999,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll be surprised and disappointed if the Dreamsouled aren\u2019t that seeing as they\u2019re approximately Wyld Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"